# SID 3000637 Dig: CORELIGHT EXPLOIT CVE-2026-70111 mup.sys DFS NameList Referral DoS

Run order: 0 → 7. Set the time picker to cover the alert storm (e.g., 10/13 16:30–16:45 for a fast first pass, then widen).

**Payload offsets used below** (`payload_printable` is 1 char per byte, 1-indexed):

| Position | Bytes | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 1–4 | NetBIOS session header | `…V` = length (V = 0x56 low byte) |
| 5–8 | `FE 53 4D 42` | `.SMB` (SMB2 magic) |
| 69 | IOCTL StructureSize | `1` = 0x31 response, `9` = 0x39 request |
| 125+ | DFS referral entries and strings | UTF-16 names print as `D.C.0.1.` |

---

## 0. Suricata src_ip Orientation Check

Negative control: is `src_ip` the packet sender or the flow originator? If it's ~100% `yes` across many SIDs, `src_ip` is flow-oriented and can't show packet direction.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight
| eval src_is_orig=if(src_ip=='id.orig_h',"yes","no")
| stats count dc(alert.signature_id) AS sids by src_is_orig
```

Also open one raw event and look for `alert.direction` or `flow.*` fields; these carry true packet direction if present.

---

## 1. SID 3000637 – Direction and IOCTL Type

Payload-based request vs. response split. `pkt_dir` shows `alert.direction` if Corelight populates it, otherwise `field_absent`.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight alert.signature_id=3000637
| eval hdr_aligned=if(substr(payload_printable,6,3)=="SMB","yes","no")
| eval ioctl_type=case(hdr_aligned=="no","not_aligned",
    substr(payload_printable,69,1)=="1","response (0x31)",
    substr(payload_printable,69,1)=="9","request (0x39)",
    true(),"other")
| eval pkt_dir=coalesce('alert.direction',"field_absent")
| stats count AS alerts dc(id.orig_h) AS clients dc(id.resp_h) AS servers by ioctl_type pkt_dir
| sort 0 - alerts
```

First run: majority `response (0x31)`, 2 `not_aligned`.

---

## 2. SID 3000637 – Receiving Client Inventory

Who received the referrals (the would-be victims). Expect Nessus scanners.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight alert.signature_id=3000637
| rename id.orig_h_name.vals{} AS client_name
| stats count AS alerts dc(id.resp_h) AS servers_contacted min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen values(client_name) AS client_name by id.orig_h
| sort 0 - alerts
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
```

---

## 3. SID 3000637 – Responder Inventory

The servers answering referrals. Bucket them into DC / DFSN root, NAS / Samba (msdfs), or other.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight alert.signature_id=3000637
| rename id.resp_h_name.vals{} AS server_name
| stats count AS alerts dc(id.orig_h) AS clients min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen values(server_name) AS server_name by id.resp_h
| sort 0 - alerts
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
```

Optional, after the stats (enrich after aggregation): `| lookup <your_asset_lookup> ip AS id.resp_h OUTPUT role`

