## 4. SID 3000637 – Referral Name String Check

Legit referrals carry UTF-16 DC/domain names; the exploit condition is an empty expanded name.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight alert.signature_id=3000637
| eval ref_body=substr(payload_printable,125)
| rex field=ref_body "(?<utf16_run>(?:[A-Za-z0-9_$-]\.){4,})"
| eval has_names=if(isnotnull(utf16_run),"yes","no")
| eval first_name=replace(utf16_run,"\.","")
| eval pkt_len=len(payload_printable)
| stats count AS alerts dc(id.resp_h) AS responders values(first_name) AS sample_names by has_names pkt_len
| sort 0 - alerts
```

Caveat: this only sees the packet that alerted. If the response spans TCP segments, the names can sit in the next segment, so `no` means "pull the pcap," not "exploit."

