## 5. SID 3000637 – Pcap Pull List

Events with no name strings, plus the `not_aligned` events the fixed offsets can't read.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight alert.signature_id=3000637
| eval ref_body=substr(payload_printable,125)
| eval reason=case(substr(payload_printable,6,3)!="SMB","not_aligned",
    NOT match(ref_body,"(?:[A-Za-z0-9_$-]\.){4,}"),"no_name_strings")
| where isnotnull(reason)
| table _time reason id.orig_h id.resp_h id.resp_p community_id spcap.url payload_printable
| sort 0 - _time
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(_time)
```

In the pcap: Wireshark filter `smb2.ioctl.function == 0x00060194`, expand the DFS referral entry, and check NumberOfExpandedNames and the first expanded name. Empty (`00 00`) is the exploit condition.

