## 6. SID 3000637 – Post-Alert Crash Indicators (conn.log)

The reboot signature on alerting clients: S1 sessions that never closed, then RSTs once the host returns with no state.

```spl
index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_conn conn_state IN ("S1","RSTR","RSTRH")
    [ search index=corelight sourcetype=corelight_suricata_corelight alert.signature_id=3000637
      | stats count by id.orig_h
      | rename id.orig_h AS id.resp_h
      | fields id.resp_h ]
| bin _time span=5m
| stats count(eval(conn_state="S1")) AS s1 count(eval(conn_state="RSTR" OR conn_state="RSTRH")) AS rst by _time id.resp_h
| where rst>=10
| sort 0 - rst
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(_time)
```

Confirm `corelight_conn` is your conn sourcetype name before running. `rst>=10` is a starting threshold; tune it to your baseline.

